WEBVTT

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.176
But the good news is,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.793
we don't need to dispose of 100 percent

00:05:33.817 --> 00:05:37.829
of the carbon dioxide we generate
from burning fossil fuels right away.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.656
Economists talk about
cost-effective pathways,

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.436
by which they mean
ways of achieving a result

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.725
without unfairly dumping
too much of the cost

00:05:46.749 --> 00:05:48.469
onto the next generation.

00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:50.936
And a cost-effective pathway,

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.206
which gets us to
decarbonizing fossil fuels,

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:58.256
100 percent carbon capture
and storage by 2050,

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.160
which is what net-zero means,